+    /*
+     * Junos evaluates the policies of the matching from-zone/to-zone pair
+     * in order, then falls through to the default policy. Global policies
+     * are consulted AFTER zone-pair policies, not before -- so the
+     * anti-spoofing deny cannot be one global rule at the top. It is
+     * repeated as the first policy of each pair instead, which costs
+     * nothing because Junos does not cap policy count.
+     */
