+   /*
+    * MTU, and the one place this profile cannot match the rest of the lab.
+    *
+    * The fabric runs an IP MTU of 9214. Junos counts MTU including the 14-byte
+    * Ethernet header, so matching it would need 9228 -- and vSRX rejects that:
+    *
+    *   Value 9228 is not within range (256..9192)
+    *
+    * 9192 is the platform maximum, which is an IP MTU of 9178: 36 bytes short
+    * of the fabric. A full-size 9214-byte packet from a host therefore does
+    * not fit through the firewall, and the symptom is the expensive one this
+    * lab warns about everywhere else -- ping works, sessions establish, bulk
+    * transfers stall with data stuck in Send-Q.
+    *
+    * `security flow tcp-mss` below is what makes that safe rather than
+    * theoretical: the firewall rewrites the MSS in every TCP handshake it
+    * forwards, so endpoints never build a segment too large for the path
+    * instead of relying on PMTUD and ICMP getting back to them through a
+    * default-deny firewall.
+    */
    fxp0 { ... }
