-  /*
-   * Static, deliberately. The border leaf points a default route in each tenant
-   * VRF at this firewall, and the firewall points the tenant prefixes back at the
-   * leaf. Running BGP here instead would be more realistic and would also hide
-   * the service-insertion path behind a protocol -- the static routes make it
-   * obvious that traffic leaves the fabric and comes back.
-   *
-   * These live in the default routing instance. fxp0 is in mgmt_junos (init.conf
-   * sets `management-instance`), so the management default route cannot leak into
-   * the transit table and steal tenant traffic.
-   */
   routing-options { ... }

